      "role": "user",
      "content": "mounier is interesting but he feels too radical for what i'm feeling. i don't feel like a revolutionary, i feel like the person the revolutionaries had to talk to. \n\nit's almost like i have this muscle memory of writing specific types of letters... very precise, very guarded. i remember the feeling of being present in these private salons, listening to the tension build between the nobles and the reformers, and being the one who had to translate those tensions into something actionable. \n\nis there anyone else? maybe someone who worked in the shadows of the ministry or as a specialized attaché? i feel like if i just find the right name, it's going to click and i'll finally understand why these memories are so strong. help me find that connection.",
